b/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:6df993056b2def17b4049d7a7e3fe2d5fa3cc9687e65e6a553d16449aa7515cd","file":"preprints/A-Counterexample-to-the-Infinite-Matroid-Packing-Covering-Conjecture-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":103,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"20daa93c3eebcc43955a89a1f66e576eb3a1de533fec7876fee11593209781b5","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-Counterexample-to-the-Infinite-Matroid-Packing-Covering-Conjecture-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:6df993056b2def17b4049d7a7e3fe2d5fa3cc9687e65e6a553d16449aa7515cd","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-Counterexample-to-the-Infinite-Matroid-Packing-Covering-Conjecture-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L103"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:intersection}\nThe same pair $(M_0,M_1)$ constructed in Theorem~\\ref{thm:main} consists of\npartitional matroids and does not satisfy intersection. More explicitly,\nfor every set $J$ independent in both $M_0$ and $M_1$ and every partition\n$J=J_0\\dot\\cup J_1$,\n\\[\n \\cl_{M_0}(J_0)\\cup\\cl_{M_1}(J_1)\\ne E.\n\\]\nConsequently, the unrestricted infinite Matroid Intersection Conjecture is\nfalse in ZFC. The pair also gives a negative ZFC answer to Jo\\'o's\nQuestion~1.5 for two partitional matroids on a common countable ground set."}
